Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://github.com/FreeSpacenav/spacenavd/issues/30

Package: spnav-onshape-bridge
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, spacenavd
Recommends: libnss3-tools
Description: Onshape 3D-mouse bridge for spacenavd
 Lets Onshape (and other web apps using the same 3Dconnexion browser API)
 use a spacenavd-driven 3D mouse on Linux, in both Chromium and Firefox.
 .
 Bridges spacenavd's motion events to the local WAMP-over-WebSocket API
 Onshape's client expects from the (Windows-only) proprietary 3Dconnexion
 driver. Generates its own per-install TLS certificate; every WebSocket
 upgrade is checked against an Origin allow-list. See
 /usr/share/doc/spnav-onshape-bridge/README.md for the full setup, including
 the browser extension/userscript and certificate trust steps that cannot
 be automated by this package alone.
